{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":19544067,"ns":0,"title":"Acyclic model","extract":"In algebraic topology, a discipline within mathematics, the acyclic models theorem can be used to show that two homology theories are isomorphic. The theorem was developed by topologists Samuel Eilenberg and Saunders MacLane.","description":"Generalizes showing that two homology theories are isomorphic","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}